diff --git a/docs/TURNIP_DARWIN_CAPTURE.md b/docs/TURNIP_DARWIN_CAPTURE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1ba03fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/TURNIP_DARWIN_CAPTURE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Darwin Turnip GPU capture
+
+`patches/mesa/turnip-darwin-perfetto-capture.patch` adds a bounded consumer to
+Mesa u_trace. `NativeAdrenoTrace.h` comes from the selected kernel ABI directory.
+The SM-T733 resolved driver directory is a symlink to the device repository,
+so both ABI headers enter the same include directory. A Darwin build whose
+kernel ABI lacks the trace header keeps the disabled callback implementations.
+
+The transport thread polls capture state every 10 ms and registers one producer
+for each active generation. It sends at most eight 176-byte events per IOKit
+call. GPU and Metal callbacks append to a 2048-event CPU queue. Each device
+accepts at most 8192 GPU trace events per generation and 64 recorded primary
+command buffers awaiting submission. Timestamp allocation uses 64-entry chunks.
+Overflow increments the explicit dropped count. Capture stop closes admission,
+drains submitted u_trace work, sends remaining records, and ends the producer.
+A three-second drain timeout reports an incomplete producer.
+
+The A6xx timestamp command is Mesa's `CP_EVENT_WRITE(RB_DONE_TS)`. Mesa waits for
+the native completion receipt before reading the timestamp BO. The conversion
+uses integer quotient and remainder at 19.2 MHz. A missing timestamp or failed
+completion wait marks the event invalid. No new CPU register access occurs.
+
+The default points include render pass, binning, sysmem/tile draw, compute,
+copy/clear, GMEM load/store, main-stream cache flushes, and the final tile store
+IB. Individual draw timing stays disabled. GMEM load/store reuse Mesa's render
+pass timestamp cloning. During capture, A6xx performs the existing tile-tail
+WFI before that clone, then emits the clone's WAIT_FOR_ME and CP_MEMCPY. The
+move crosses only the timestamp-copy commands; draw, final store, and the tile
+render-end marker retain their ordering. Outside capture the original command
+sequence remains. The instrumentation event records encoded timestamp,
+CP_MEMCPY, WAIT_FOR_ME, and additional WFI dword counts. These counters describe
+capture commands; they do not measure shader or cache execution time.
+
+Each command-buffer recording receives a process-wide monotonically increasing
+ID. Metal metadata converts its Vulkan handle to that ID. The submit event
+associates the recording ID with Turnip's submission number plus one and the
+kernel completion receipt. Execute-secondary events associate secondary IDs
+with the primary. Begin and end GPU events share point, name, and recording ID.
+The shared ABI header lists Turnip point and argument IDs. Metal metadata uses
+point IDs 1 through 7, argument key `point * 16 + argument_index`, and source
+flags in event flags bits 16 through 31.
+
+The host owns Perfetto protobuf encoding and GPU/CPU clock alignment. GPU
+intervals represent completed render-backend timestamps; subtraction between
+neighboring stages alone does not identify a pure wait interval.
diff --git a/docs/drivers/adreno-metal.md b/docs/drivers/adreno-metal.md
index 79b7bca..763e688 100644
--- a/docs/drivers/adreno-metal.md
+++ b/docs/drivers/adreno-metal.md
@@ -28,6 +28,50 @@ A render pass that cannot be encoded still returns an encoder, and its command
 buffer is refused: RenderBox caches encoder methods and cannot take nil. The first problem of each process is written to the driver's
 per-process text line from the thread that hit it.
 
+The selected board supplies the same `NativeAdrenoABI.h` to Turnip and the plugin.
+Turnip reads the reported ABI version and sends 16 indirect buffers in a 416-byte
+record for version 1, or 128 in a 3104-byte record for version 2. The diagnostic
+mailbox retains the 16-buffer record. Host-import pages remain retained until the
+kernel acknowledges removal of their GPU mapping.
+
+On a Darwin device advertising cached coherent memory, Turnip exposes that memory
+as the default type for resources, heaps and internal command storage. CPU maps
+use write-back caching, and the kernel selects GPU mapping attributes from the
+allocation or imported pages. Metal Shared storage, WriteCombined hints, Private
+resources and eagerly allocated Memoryless attachments prefer cached coherent
+memory on unified-memory GPUs. The frontend's device query recognizes hardware
+coherence and kernel-managed visibility; either removes IOSurface flush-range
+collection and userspace cache operations from submission and completion.
+
+The SM7325 adaptation passes resource declarations, render memory barriers and
+fence stages through the frontend into metal2vulkan. Encoding accumulates access
+summaries, and submission exports GPU writes to the CPU only for allocations
+with CPU consumers. Turnip's asynchronous Darwin extension submits timeline
+dependencies and output points to the kernel scheduler; CPU waits sleep on the
+requested point. Display holds a read of the IOSurface backing until DPU has
+switched to its replacement.
+
+The `unixnu-sm-t733` branch keeps these submission and synchronization changes
+with the system BGRA8 sRGB format policy. The `unixnu-sm-t733-apple3` branch adds
+the Apple3 frontend, compiler and format implementations. Each device branch
+pins its corresponding core, SoC and Metal revisions.
+
+The SM7325 bridge uses metal2vulkan development commit
+`624bab3918de5b978e1101517abca2b4fa426565` and the ordered patches in
+`AdrenoMetal/bridge/patches/series`. The new runtime's fence stages retain the
+local resource visibility and cached coherent memory policies.
+
+Device answers are cached by selector and argument. The frontend disables no-copy
+rebind replay logs. Host-page textures use their imported memory directly when
+the runtime accepts the layout. Turnip uses draw loads and 2D stores for linear
+imported attachments whose dimensions do not fill complete GMEM blocks. Those
+transfers cover the valid texels within the owner's row pitch.
+
+Frame trace and pipeline journal files default off through
+`NATIVE_ADRENO_FRAME_TRACE=0` and `NATIVE_ADRENO_PIPELINE_JOURNAL=0`. Periodic
+in-memory statistics remain available. Frontend and host-import release errors
+each print at most 32 entries per process.
+
 ```sh
 python3 scripts/build-turnip-darwin.py --target ios
 python3 scripts/build-adreno-metal-plugin.py
diff --git a/docs/drivers/arm-smmu4k.md b/docs/drivers/arm-smmu4k.md
index ccc4cde..f900306 100644
--- a/docs/drivers/arm-smmu4k.md
+++ b/docs/drivers/arm-smmu4k.md
@@ -12,6 +12,11 @@ ARM SMMUv2 native 4 KiB table kit. Builds and programs stage-1/stage-2 context t
 
 Used by Adreno740 and the storage drivers.
 
+`coherent_walk = 1` configures outer-shareable WBWA table reads. The platform
+retains CPU write-back table memory and uses the publication callback to order
+CPU stores before device access. Live updates retain their TLB invalidation
+and synchronization sequence.
+
 Live updates map or unmap a batch of pages in one transaction: one page publication, one TLB synchronization and one recheck per batch. `ArmSmmu4KLiveMapContextBatchExclusive` maps pages the caller owns exclusively and skips the alias check against the existing ranges; the changes are still checked against each other. An unmap of up to 512 pages invalidates each removed page with TLBIVAL; a larger unmap invalidates the ASID.
 
 ## Build
